# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: cador-3-host-interface-protocol-spec — D1 host-interface spec + formal autolisp↔host protocol + D2 cador spec
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: spec
#+DEPENDS: cador-multidocument-host
#+BRANCH: cador

* Context

Sub-task 3 of the =cador-multidocument-host= epic — its deliverables
D1, D2, D5 (§3, §4, §5). Writing the specification and design, including
the *formal definition of the protocol between AutoLISP and the host*.

* Problem

The host interface is clautolisp's single way out to CAD/GUI (epic §1),
but it is only implemented (as CLOS generics =host-*=), not specified.
The cador multidocument runtime (cador-2) and any future wire host need a
backend-agnostic, formally-defined contract to implement against.

* Proposal / deliverables

- **D1 — =clautolisp-host-interface-spec.org=.** The generic, backend-
  agnostic host interface. Operations by group (epic §4): session/document
  management; database/entity access; system variables + scope tiers;
  interaction + the *console device* (explicitly not a cl:stream); command
  layer; filesystem/encoding; notification/reactors; concurrency/locking.
  Plus the two cross-cutting mechanisms — capability query, and the
  condition taxonomy (not-supported-by-this-host vs unavailable-headless
  vs not-yet-implemented vs backend-error). Close with the fidelity matrix
  (rows = operations; columns = nihil, cador, <wire-host>, AutoCAD,
  BricsCAD).
- **Formal protocol.** A precise definition of the request/response
  contract between the AutoLISP engine and a host: message/operation set,
  argument and result value domains, error signalling, ordering and the
  park/resume interaction (so it holds for an in-image host, cador's
  coroutine model, and a future out-of-process wire host alike). This is
  the artefact cador-2's scheduler and any wire host implement.
- **D2 — =clautolisp-cador-spec.org=.** Part I semantics (session model,
  scheduler/parking, current-vs-active document, namespace/symbol model,
  blackboard, sysvar scope tiers, handles, streams/encoding, startup hook
  chain, the headless console device, deliberate omissions) — each a
  stated decision, not a survey. Part II design (DB backend choice,
  command-layer scope, debugger integration surfaces, module/package
  layout). Resolve every §5 and §9 open question with a provenance grade;
  every assumption in a dedicated subsection.
- **D5 — naming + architecture note** recording epic §1 (may be a D1
  section) so the decision survives the epic.

Conventions per epic §3 (org-mode, provenance grades A/B/C/V, assumptions
flagged). Documents live under =clautolisp/documentation/=.

* Acceptance criteria

- [ ] D1 exists, backend-agnostic, with the fidelity matrix and the
      capability-query + condition-taxonomy mechanisms.
- [ ] The formal autolisp↔host protocol is defined precisely enough for
      cador-2 and a future wire host to implement against it.
- [ ] D2 Part I + Part II reach a stated decision on every §5 / §9 item.
- [ ] Constraints C1–C8 each trace to a D2 section.

* Notes

D1 must be specifiable without reference to any particular host (epic §3).
Feeds cador-1 (the condition taxonomy nihil/cador use) and cador-2 (the
protocol the scheduler realises).

* Decisions and refresh — 2026-09-28

pjb decided the two D1 design questions:

- *§14 capability query: none.* Capability stays implicit (invoke, handle the
  condition); =host-capable-p= would be an extension, and extensions are
  minimised.
- *§15 condition taxonomy: a superclass and four subclasses* -- =host-error=
  over not-supported-by-this-host / unavailable-in-headless-context /
  not-yet-implemented / backend-error -- so errors can be caught globally or
  specifically. Implementation tracked in cador-4.

Both documents were refreshed against cador-2 (closed the same day) and moved
to DOCUMENT_VERSION 0.2.0, still "draft for review":

- =clautolisp/documentation/clautolisp-host-interface-spec.org= (D1 + D5) --
  §3 Group 1 now states the built generics, §10/§13 the built parking model
  (threads on condition variables), §12 matrix rows updated, §14/§15 decided,
  §19 records the refresh.
- =clautolisp/documentation/clautolisp-cador-spec.org= (D2) -- §I.1/§I.2/§II.14
  refreshed, §9.5/§9.6 updated, the "analysis document not found" note
  corrected (it exists), a 2026-09-28 refresh section at the end.

What remains for pjb's review: sign-off of the D1 fidelity-matrix rows and
section structure, and the D2 Part II decisions + epic §5/§9 items. Nothing
blocks that review any more.
